menu "MQTT broker"

    config MINIHUB_MQTT_BROKER
        bool "Enable on-device MQTT broker"
        default y
        help
            Run an mosquitto broker on the Hub (TCP 1883) so MQTT devices at
            the site connect to the Hub itself instead of a separate always-on
            machine. The broker is a pure transport service: it carries no Hub
            points. At run time adapters.mqtt_broker.enabled decides whether it
            listens (factory seed: off), and that same flag starts the Hub's own
            loopback MQTT client, which is what host.mqtt rides on. Turning this
            option off therefore also drops CONFIG_MINIHUB_MQTT_ADAPTER and
            CONFIG_MINIHUB_JS_MQTT: a product without an on-device broker has no
            MQTT client either.

            After flipping this option in an existing build directory, build
            twice (or run reconfigure first). The component manager evaluates
            the espressif/mosquitto rule against build/config/sdkconfig.json,
            which kconfgen only writes later in the same configure pass, so the
            first build still sees the previous value and drops the package:
            "mosq_broker.h: No such file or directory". Turning the option off
            needs no second pass, and a fresh build directory resolves in one.

endmenu
